cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BASTION in academic work, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "BASTION: Lock-Step, Staggered and Sequential Share Schedules for a First-Order Masked ML-KEM NTT on FPGA"
abstract: >-
  RTL, testbenches, KAT vectors and synthesis scripts for BASTION, a
  first-order arithmetic-masked Number Theoretic Transform core for ML-KEM
  (FIPS 203) on FPGA with spatially separated share domains, and for its
  unmasked reference configurations.
authors:
  - family-names: "Lázaro Díaz"
    given-names: "Marcos"
    affiliation: "Universidad Politécnica de Madrid"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/m-lazaro/bastion-ntt"
